# common-knowledge skill

Invocation: `/ck <command> [project]` or `/common-knowledge <command> [project]`

## Commands
- `init` — Create and initialize the knowledge store at ~/common-knowledge
- `save <project> [--section <area>] [--auto]` — Save current context to a project
- `load <project> [--section <area>]` — Load all knowledge for a project
- `map <project>` — Generate/update codebase map
- `schema <project>` — Save DB schema or API spec
- `progress <project>` — Append timestamped progress entry
- `link <a> <b> [--type <rel>]` — Record cross-project connection
- `learn "<text>" [project] [--type <t>] [--tags <csv>]` — Capture a gotcha/pattern/pitfall/insight/idea
- `learnings [project] [--tag <t>]` — Recall saved learnings into context
- `ingest <file> [project]` — Extract a PDF/CSV/DOCX/PPTX/XLSX and distill it into the store
- `status` — List all tracked projects
- `search <query>` — Full-text search across the store
- `sync` — Git commit all pending changes

## Key Rules
- Store location: `$CK_HOME` (default: `~/common-knowledge` on macOS/Linux)
- Every write is a git commit with a descriptive message
- `progress.md` and `connections.md` are append-only — never overwrite
- `meta.json` must always be valid JSON
- Use `--auto` to auto-detect project from cwd

